WHO CAN USE IT

You have a license if you've completed at least 30 consecutive days of paid
membership in the AI Era community (https://www.skool.com/ai-era), or you
bought Architectural Guardrail directly from us. Otherwise you have no rights
to this code, however you got hold of it, and you should delete it.

Once you've completed that first paid month, the version you have is yours
permanently. You don't need to stay subscribed to keep using it. You're just
not entitled to future versions, updates, fixes, or support — those come with
an active membership at the time we release them.


WHAT YOU CAN DO

Build anything you want. Unlimited products, SaaS you charge for, client and
agency work, internal tools. Modify it, rewrite it, swap out the stack, deploy
it anywhere. Sell a business you built on it (the buyer needs their own
license to keep developing the code; we take no equity and no cut). Put
employees and contractors on it, under NDA, with you responsible for them.

No attribution needed. Build your own brand.


WHAT YOU CAN'T DO

Give the Software away. That's the whole of it, but specifically: don't sell,
sublicense, publish, or distribute it or any substantial part of it; don't put
it in a public repo or share it on Discord, Telegram, forums, or file hosts;
don't repackage it as a template, starter kit, or course asset; don't release
it for free; don't teach others to rebuild it through tutorials, courses, or
"how it's built" content; don't use the name "Architectural Guardrail" in
anything your customers see; don't strip the copyright headers; and don't let
anyone without a license see the source.

Shipping a product built on this to your users is fine and expected. Handing
someone the code is not.


OPEN SOURCING YOUR OWN PRODUCT

We're not against open source. You can open source a product you built on this,
as long as what you publish is your product and not our system. The test is
simple: if someone could clone your repo and have a working copy of
Architectural Guardrail, you've redistributed our codebase — no matter what
license you attached or what you named it.

So you can't publish the Software (or a substantial part of it) under MIT,
Apache, GPL, or anything else; can't publish something that presents itself as
Architectural Guardrail or borrows the name; can't publish this codebase with
the branding swapped; and can't split it across repos to get around this.

Putting an open source license on code you don't own doesn't make it open
source. Not sure if something crosses the line? Ask us first.


KEEPING IT PRIVATE

Private repos, real access controls, NDAs for anyone you let in. You're fully
responsible for everyone you give access to. If it leaks, tell us immediately.


OWNERSHIP

We own the Software. Your license is non-exclusive and non-transferable — it
can't be resold or shared with a partner or co-founder, who'd need their own.
We may license this to any number of other people.

What you build on top is yours: your features, your product, your business.
But since the result is built on our code, this license still governs the
whole of it.


NO REFUNDS, NO CHARGEBACKS

All sales are final. Once you have the code you have the intellectual
property, so refunds aren't possible. You can cancel your membership anytime,
but periods already paid for aren't refunded.

Requesting a refund, filing a chargeback, or reversing the payment that made
you eligible is itself a violation of this license. Your license is void
immediately and permanently, you lose all rights to the Software, and you must
delete every copy. A later membership won't restore it.

You also owe us 30% of the reversed amount as liquidated damages for the
administrative and recovery costs a reversal creates, on top of any chargeback
fees, processing costs, and collection or legal costs we incur. We may process
that automatically.


TERMINATION

We can terminate your license if you break these terms — leaking or
redistributing the code, teaching others to build it, using our name on your
product, or requesting a refund or chargeback. We can't revoke it just because
we changed our minds. On termination, stop using the Software and delete your
copies, with no refund.


